---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base title="Support" description="Get help with Posato on Mac and iPhone.">
  <div class="prose">
    <h1>Support</h1>
    <p class="lead">Send questions, problems, or ideas about Posato on Mac or iPhone to the addresses below.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Help with Posato: <a href="mailto:support@posato.app">support@posato.app</a></li>
      <li>Privacy questions: <a href="mailto:privacy@posato.app">privacy@posato.app</a></li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Share only what you need to describe the problem. You don't need to include website names, app
      names, device details, screenshots, or logs. Replies are best effort.
    </p>

    <h2>Before you write</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Mac:</strong> Posato must stay open. Starting or resuming blocking needs administrator
        approval. Website blocking covers Safari and Google Chrome Stable while they use the system proxy settings.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>iPhone:</strong> Restrictions can linger after a session ends. For sessions under 15
        minutes, they clear only when Posato is open at the end or the next time you open it.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Sync:</strong> Sync is best effort; a change may arrive late or not at all. If every copy of your workspace key is lost,
        synchronized data cannot be recovered.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      The <a href="/limits/">full limits</a> cover browser coverage, VPN and Private Relay behavior, resuming after sleep, and data recovery.
    </p>
    <p>
      You can always end a session early or remove Posato. See the <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a> for what Posato keeps on your devices and in iCloud.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
